  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>We know that the sum of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;terms of an arithmetic progression with its first term as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and common difference&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>530</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>530</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>106</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Subtracting the two equation, we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>On putting the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;in the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>20</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>175</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>175</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1862</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
